        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69354,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69355,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal pelvis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69356,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>ORTI has no specific clinical presentation, but most patients present with gross haematuria and a calcified mass protruding into the renal pelvis on imaging {8597860; 24407230}. No association with any other renal tumour type or syndrome has been published.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69357,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are extremely rare, with only about 25&nbsp;cases published in the literature. There is a clear male predominance (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 7:1), and patients are aged between 6&nbsp;days and 2.5&nbsp;years {27633911; 30425880}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69358,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69359,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69360,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are well circumscribed and measure 10&ndash;60&nbsp;mm in diameter. Almost all tumours show signs of calcification on imaging studies, and this is reflected in the gross appearance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69361,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>ORTIs are composed of two cell types: osteoblast-like cells that are located between and around areas of osteoid, and a spindle cell (blastema-like) component, mostly at the periphery of the tumour {8597860}. Osteoblast-like cells and spindle cells are both bland, without features of malignancy. Immunohistochemistry shows that the osteoblast-like cells are almost always positive for EMA and vimentin {27633911}. SATB2 and WT1 have also been reported to be positive {27633911; 29187024}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69362,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69363,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Five cases of ORTI with clonal trisomy&nbsp;4 have now been reported (in two different papers), so clonal trisomy&nbsp;4 seems a relevant and recurrent molecular abnormality {22976287; 27633911}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69364,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> the typical histological combination of osteoid, osteoblastic cells, and spindle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69365,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All tumours are limited to the kidney and regarded as benign lesions. No particular staging protocol applies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69366,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a benign tumour for which conservative surgical management is sufficient. Outcome has been uniformly favourable {8597860; 9589480}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T17:08:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]